cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the paper
  describing the algorithm you used (see preferred-citation and references).
title: "catraj: Context-Aware Trajectory Processing"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementations of context-aware trajectory annotation, compression
  and prediction algorithms developed during the doctoral research of Saeed
  Mehri, compatible with the MovingPandas library. It implements trajectory
  annotation -- spatial interpolation across observation stations followed by
  temporal interpolation through time, so every trajectory point carries the
  conditions the moving object passed through -- and Context-Aware
  Douglas-Peucker (CADP) compression, which keeps the points that carry that
  context, and Context-aware Piecewise Linear Segmentation (CPLS) compression,
  which keeps the points that stop the simplified trajectory crossing a
  barrier such as a shoreline.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mehri
    given-names: Saeed
    email: sa.mehri20@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/smehri/catraj"
keywords:
  - trajectory annotation
  - context awareness
  - movement data
  - spatial interpolation

# The annotation method implemented in this release.
